  "id": "COMPOUND:17740 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Murrayaquinone A appears to interact with multiple proteins that ultimately target CHP-134 through a series of molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Murrayaquinone A acts as a target for Acacetin 7-(2G-rhamnosyl)-rutinoside and Dendridine A, both of which are known to interact with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn targets CHP-134. Similarly, Murrayaquinone A also targets Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is also a target of Taiwanin C, which also leads to CHP-134. These findings indicate that Murrayaquinone A may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a key player in the signaling network leading to CHP-134. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Murrayaquinone A to influence CHP-134 through a central molecular hub, suggesting a possible role in modulating cellular processes that ultimately affect CHP-134.",
